WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.067
[intense music]

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.002
Come on.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.937
OK.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.705
Now you got fish.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.007
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
I'm on the Tornio River,

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.844
and I've finally
caught something.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.212
It's a fish, right, Marcu?

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.314
No, it's not fish, but stone.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.015
There are only stone there.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.916
Damn.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:17.984
I thought had one, then.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:18.918
Yeah.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.053
Come on, baby.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.655
[intense music]

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.159
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): The river is

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.461
clearly not in a giving mood.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.563
Maybe today is
not my lucky day.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.398
Yeah.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.599
Listen, what I'd love to do--

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.566
Yeah.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.834
If you don't
mind, is taste one.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.236
Yeah.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.538
And we have a special way
to cook this whitefish.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.472
That's hard.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.306
Yeah.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:40.940
A lot harder than you think.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:41.541
Yeah.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.742
Exactly.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.544
It's quite unique to
be given a chance to fish

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.447
with this family because only
a few families have the rights

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.715
to fish along these banks.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.650
So a unique experience.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:54.487
I just hate going
home empty handed.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.256
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Marcu has asked

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.125
his friend Kimmo teach
me the traditional way

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.193
to cook whitefish.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.494
We're gonna taste it in here.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.029
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
This being Finland,

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.598
it obviously involves
a very warm wooden hut.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:06.533
Hello.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.100
Hello.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.067
How are you?

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:08.968
Oh, Kimmo.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:09.569
Kimmo, nice to see you.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.270
Gordon.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:10.904
Wow, this is beautiful.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.638
Yeah.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.006
Oh my God.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.240
So traditionally, they're all
cooked on sticks like that?

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.142
Yeah, this is traditional way.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.710
Couple hundred years.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.746
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER): The
fish are rested for 24 hours

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:24.117
before they're cooked and then
put on this open fire to roast.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.785
He's turning them
round every, what,

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:26.753
every three or four minutes?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.654
Yeah.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.087
Once they're colored?

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:28.855
Yeah.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.023
That's amazing.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.925
And what are you
seasoning them with?

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:32.859
What's the seasoning?

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.526
Just natural.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.093
No.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.028
Nothing before.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:35.662
Nothing at all.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.095
Wow.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:36.930
Hello.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:37.831
Well, let me show.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.465
Golden.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.032
Wow.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:39.799
That's golden.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:40.567
This is ready.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.134
They're ready.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.135
It's crispy.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:42.769
What's he putting in there?

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.470
Yeah.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.037
This is--

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:44.938
What is that?

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.473
Very strong salt water.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.641
And that's the only
way you prepare it.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.376
And after it's ready.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.512
So he cools them down
in the salted water?

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.580
Yeah.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.381
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): The saltwater

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.917
prevents them from cooking any
further and flavors the fish.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.052
What an amazing technique.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.186
They look incredible.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.054
The smell--

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:01.821
Yeah.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.056
-- is amazing.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:03.890
Kimmo, how do you
know they're cooked?

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.458
[speaking finnish]

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.660
He has a thermometer
on his finger.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.228
Right.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.462
He's got therm--

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.730
You've made the skin
almost like bacon.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.364
It's crispy.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:11.931
Yeah.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:12.532
Not too hard.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:13.166
No.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:13.766
But not too soft.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:14.667
No.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.101
Got a beautiful color.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.569
Crispy.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.204
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Maybe it's the chef in me,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.873
but I can't stand by and
watch Kimmo do all the work

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.374
without offering a hand.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.942
Kimmo, do you
want them turned?

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:23.843
Yeah?

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.378
Which ones?

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.112
This.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:26.813
Turn that one.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.647
And this.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.915
Man.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.816
Ah?

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.550
It's the water.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:31.451
It's ready.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.185
In?

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.686
And next one.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.054
[bleep] You got to move fast
because all of a sudden--

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:35.855
Crispy.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.390
This one?

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.458
You start off with nothing,
and then they're all going.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.792
This one?

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.728
Check.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.662
That's helpful, hey.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.730
[speaking finnish]

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:44.464
Yes.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:44.998
Fast, fast.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:45.698
Fast, fast.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:46.199
Coming up.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.233
Coming up.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.902
[speaking finnish]

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:49.903
Oh.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:50.837
That one.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:51.571
That one.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:52.539
Go, go.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:53.273
Go, go.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.941
[bleep] Go fast.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:55.875
This one?

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.644
Oh, [bleep].

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.578
Oh.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:02:59.946
[bleep]

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:00.980
Last two.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.415
Kimmo, two to go.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:03.349
Yeah?

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.584
One each, because
you've done no--

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.552
you've done no work.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.252
Yeah.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:06.986
You just stood there.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:07.620
Yeah, I'm--

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.454
Yes.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.088
But I am the fisherman, too.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:09.989
Yeah.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:10.924
[bleep]

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.858
Really?

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:12.892
Seriously?

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:13.793
Last one.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.994
Look at that.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:15.929
Great.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:16.963
[gentle music]

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:17.664
Kimmo.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.598
Oh.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:19.699
Please may we eat now?

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.600
Yes.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.869
Thank you.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.337
God, look how white that is.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.038
Oh?

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.839
No, there's no bone.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.807
Mm.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:28.775
[speaking finnish]

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.944
Oh my goodness, me.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.278
It doesn't need salt, Kimmo.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.613
It is really delicious.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.814
Honestly.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.683
It's the only village you
can get it in the world.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:37.116
Really?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.685
Yeah.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.553
I've eaten a lot of fish in
my life, sometimes with chips.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.522
But that on its
own is delicious.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.925
And it's given me a lot of
inspiration for the final cook

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.493
at the end of the week.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.662
And I'd love for both of you
to join us at the final cook.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:50.597
Really?

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:51.664
OK.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.366
Now, would you do
me a favor and go out

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.100
and get some fish for the
cook at the end of the week?

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.301
Yeah.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.936
Let's say, I do
immediately after this.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:57.937
Will you catch any this time?

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:58.871
Yeah.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.106
For sure.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.074
Delicious.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.808
Thank you.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:02.709
Great job.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.409
What an amazing fish.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.377
Delicious.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.578
It's definitely
given me inspiration

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.679
now for the final cook.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.414
Don't get too clever
with this white fish.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.650
First of all, I'm going to
have to follow that technique

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.152
and cook over wood, otherwise
if you start filleting it,

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.088
cooking it skin side
down, nonstick pan,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.723
you're going to get
absolutely slaughtered.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:22.929
So keep it simple, but a nice
little find, the whitefish.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:27.634
[thoughtful music]

